  X some proteomes have 35,000+ genes, although we currently can
    filter on the geneIDs, this resets any genes selected so far.  We
    need to have a way of creating a custom list by successive
    browsing and searching.  

    Here is an example use-case:

      By default you see the first page of top hits, let's say you
      select 3 of those, but then you think of a particular gene
      you're interested, then search for that, and add it to the list,
      and now you've got 4 genes.  Once you finalize the list, then
      you'd press "Submit" to generate the final PDF.

    Possible interface implementation idea: would be to adding a new
    pane (perhaps above or below the current list) that keeps track of
    the genes selected so far, those added either via browsing the
    pages, or by searching the geneIDs.

